<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Greco-Turkish War (1919–1922)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1919">1919</a>–<a href="/years/1922">1922</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkish-war-of-independence">Turkish War of Independence</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Greco-Turkish War of 1919–1922 was fought between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> and the Turkish nationalist movement after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>. Greek forces landed at Smyrna in 1919 and advanced deep into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, but were stopped at the Sakarya in 1921 and routed in 1922; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-lausanne">Treaty of Lausanne</a> (1923) and a population exchange followed, ending the Greek presence in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia-minor">Asia Minor</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/greco-turkish-war-1919-1922.jpg" alt="Greco-Turkish War (1919–1922)" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Crasyy · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Greco-Turkish_War_of_1919-1922_collage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
